# Random modules with type classes, some with superclasses or two
# parameters, instances for type constructors with and without constraints
# whose methods call methods on their parts, and predicates and functions
# with class constraints that call methods and each other at types that the
# callers' constraints or the instances satisfy
# (generate-polymorphic-programs.py --classes). merkc must give each
# procedure, instance methods included, the hidden type_info and
# typeclass_info arguments that mmc does, find its constrained type
# variables' type_infos where mmc does, and pass each call the same
# typeclass_infos, made the same way.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-polymorphic-programs.py --classes --seed 17 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-polymorphism %t/*.m
